A crystalline geometric structure emerging from morning mist, rendered in the style of Piet Mondrian with bold primary colors (red, yellow, blue) and stark black grid lines. The crystal formation is composed of intersecting rectangular planes at dynamic angles, suggesting clarity and precision. The background features soft gradients of white and pale gray, creating depth. Small, jewel-like facets catch light throughout the composition, represented as pure color blocks. The overall feeling is one of elegant simplicity and organized structure emerging from complexity—clean, methodical, yet surprisingly human and approachable. The crystal sits on a subtle horizon line, grounded yet reaching upward with geometric confidence.
